<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarom</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarom is a mountainous district of Zanjan province in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in the valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qezel-ozan">Qezel Ozan</a> river. In the 10th century it was the home of the Daylamite Sallarid dynasty, also called the Musafirids, whose fortress of Shamiran stood there and who for a time ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. The district is known for its olive groves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarom.jpg" alt="Tarom" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Colin Cooke Photo · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YR-BGK_Boeing_737-82R_Tarom_LHR_17.1.22.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
